      "writtenOn": "2020-02-04T19:36:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this could be in this way:\n\n#ifdef BOARD_CR50\n  const int in_packet_mode \u003d ec_comm_is_uart_in_packet_mode(uart);\n#endif\n\n  ...\n\n#ifdef BOARD_CR50\n  while (uartn_rx_available(uart)) {\n    uint8_t ch;\n\n    if (!in_packet_mode)\n        if (count \u003d\u003d q_room)\n            break;\n\n    ch \u003d uartn_read_char(uart);\n\n    if (in_packet_mode)\n        if (ec_comm_process_packet(ch) || (count \u003d\u003d q_room))\n          continue;\n\n    uart_in-\u003ebuffer[tail \u0026 mask] \u003d ch;\n#else\n  while ((count !\u003d q_room) \u0026\u0026 uartn_rx_available(uart)) {\n    uart_in-\u003ebuffer[tail \u0026 mask] \u003d uartn_read_char(uart);\n#endif\n    tail++;\n    count++;\n  }\n\n\nThis version has more if-condition inside the loop. I like to keep the patch#21.",
